<title>BELGIUM: EU takes Japan to WTO over pork imports.</title>
<headline>EU takes Japan to WTO over pork imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has requested formal consultations with Japan at the World Trade Organisation over what it says are unfair practices relating to pigmeat imports.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the European Commission -- the EU's executive -- said a periodic use of emergency import restrictions by Japan since November 1995 had caused disruptions that effectively priced European pigmeat exports out of the Japanese market.</p>
<p>The Commission said Japan's &quot;failure to administer the import of frozen pigmeat in a uniform, impartial and reasonable manner&quot; contravened the terms of the Uruguay Round agreement.</p>
<p>The Commission said Canada was likely to join the EU's request for consultations.</p>
</text>
